WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:04.860
I'm Jenna Fisher.

2
00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:06.160
And I'm Angela Kinsey.

3
00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:07.440
We were on The Office together.

4
00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:08.700
And we're best friends.

5
00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:12.520
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.

6
00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:19.500
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.

7
00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:20.660
We're The Office Ladies.

8
00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:25.340
Hi, lady.

9
00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:26.200
And everyone.

10
00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:27.800
Hi, everyone out there.

11
00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:29.680
I'm so happy you're here listening.

12
00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:34.240
Jenna and I, someday we're going to come out there and take it on the road and meet you.

13
00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:35.240
Whoa!

14
00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:38.280
Oh, that's news to me.

15
00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:41.940
I guess we're doing it, though, because if Angela gets an idea, it's going to happen.

16
00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:44.800
I think we got to do one in Scranton, Jenna.

17
00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:46.040
Oh, well, that's a given.

18
00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:47.740
We got to go to Scranton.

19
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.220
We got to do an Office Ladies from Scranton.

20
00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:50.740
All right.

21
00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:52.140
It's been said.

22
00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:53.080
Now it must be done.

23
00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:55.780
Lady, tell them what we're talking about today.

24
00:00:56.480 --> 00:01:00.380
Today is Season 4, Episode 17, Job Fair.

25
00:01:00.380 --> 00:01:08.160
This was written by Lee Eisenberg and Gene Stepnitsky, writers of Dinner Party, and directed by Tucker Gates.

26
00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:09.780
Would you like a summary?

27
00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:11.340
I can't wait for your summaries.

28
00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:13.520
Like, Wednesday night, you know, because we record on Thursday.

29
00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:17.540
I go to bed and I'm like, ooh, what is Jenna's summary going to be?

30
00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:18.680
I know you do.

31
00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:19.540
I know.

32
00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:24.780
You try to text me and get me to tell you my summaries ahead of time, and I say you're just going to have to wait for it.

33
00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:25.160
Yeah.

34
00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:26.360
You want to surprise me.

35
00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:27.680
I go to bed thinking about it.

36
00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:28.860
I wake up thinking about it.

37
00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:29.900
Well, here it is.

38
00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:30.720
Wait no longer.

39
00:01:31.060 --> 00:01:31.320
Okay.

40
00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:43.740
Michael, Pam, Oscar, and Daryl attend a job fair at Pam's alma mater, Valley View High School, in search of the, quote, best and brightest potential summer interns.

41
00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:47.680
Jim is on probation at Dunder Mifflin.

42
00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:49.640
You know, he got his warning from Ryan.

43
00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:56.860
So he is going to attempt to redeem himself by working a potential client over golf with the help of Andy and Kevin.

44
00:01:57.120 --> 00:02:04.140
The rest of the Dunder Mifflin employees take the day off, despite a warning from Dwight, except for Angela,

45
00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:09.660
who ends her silent treatment of him when they find themselves alone in the office.

46
00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:10.800
It's perfect.

47
00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:12.580
That's a perfect summary.

48
00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:13.740
Thank you.

49
00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:14.740
You're welcome.

50
00:02:15.380 --> 00:02:19.460
Fast fact number one, Valley View High School, Pam's alma mater.

51
00:02:19.940 --> 00:02:20.240
Yeah.

52
00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:21.180
We got mail.

53
00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:22.300
Kavya R.

54
00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:23.420
and Courtney K.

55
00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:28.640
asked, is Valley View High School a real high school and did you film there?

56
00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:29.660
And?

57
00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:31.800
It is a real high school.

58
00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:32.720
Ding, ding, ding.

59
00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:36.700
It's about nine miles north of Scranton in the suburb of Archbold.

60
00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:39.440
Their school mascot is the Cougar.

61
00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:40.160
Mm-hmm.

62
00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:45.120
And their school colors appear to be blue and yellow, maybe blue and gold.

63
00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:46.280
Goldish yellow.

64
00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:49.240
I went to the website because it's the Cougar, right?

65
00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:50.580
So you're saying it's yellow?

66
00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:52.220
I'm saying it's goldy yellow.

67
00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:53.400
Goldish yellow.

68
00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:54.400
Okay.

69
00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:56.980
Their colors are blue and goldish yellow.

70
00:02:59.100 --> 00:02:59.700
Okay.

71
00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:04.380
We did not film at that school.

72
00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:05.220
Oh, no.

73
00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:09.440
We filmed at Birmingham High School in Van Nuys, California.

74
00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:15.780
By the way, in my research, I discovered that the music videos for Gwen Stefani's Hollaback Girl,

75
00:03:16.580 --> 00:03:22.080
Eminem's No Love, and Lil Wayne's Prom Queen have also all filmed at Birmingham High School.

76
00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:24.800
Very, very popular location.

77
00:03:25.340 --> 00:03:26.900
Well, wait for it, Angela.

78
00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:28.540
Do you know what else is filmed there?

79
00:03:28.820 --> 00:03:29.620
Oh, God.

80
00:03:29.860 --> 00:03:30.600
Oh, let me guess.

81
00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:31.100
Let me guess.

82
00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:32.600
Fast Times at Ridgemont High.

83
00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:33.200
No.

84
00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:34.160
Grease.

85
00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:36.140
It's an office connection.

86
00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:37.040
Oh.

87
00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:37.680
Hmm.

88
00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:40.320
40-Year-Old Virgin?

89
00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:42.620
An episode of Monk.

90
00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:43.740
Oh!

91
00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:47.260
An episode of Monk.

92
00:03:47.320 --> 00:03:49.600
What is it with The Office and Monk?

93
00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:50.700
I don't know.

94
00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:54.280
I really wish we had filmed back in, like, the 50s.

95
00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:57.800
Remember when they would do those crossover episodes and all of a sudden, like, Laverne

96
00:03:57.800 --> 00:04:01.680
and Shirley would be over at, you know, the Fonzie's house?

97
00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:02.440
Yeah.

98
00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:04.700
It'd be like, Happy Days, Laverne and Shirley.

99
00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:07.560
What if we had a Monk The Office crossover?

100
00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:12.820
I wish we could go back in time and make that happen, because we clearly used the same locations

101
00:04:12.820 --> 00:04:14.120
and the same guest stars.

102
00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:16.780
Have Tony Shalhoub walk into the bullpen?

103
00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:17.340
Come on.

104
00:04:17.740 --> 00:04:18.820
And interview someone.

105
00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:21.680
Maybe Toby for being the Scranton Strangler.

106
00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:22.520
Yes!

107
00:04:22.840 --> 00:04:23.740
We did it!

108
00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:24.800
We did it!

109
00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:25.960
There it is, everybody.

110
00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:29.520
Your office reunion is also a Monk crossover.

111
00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:30.240
Done.

112
00:04:30.760 --> 00:04:32.620
A little more information on the school.

113
00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:36.780
The school colors for Birmingham High School appear to be blue and white.

114
00:04:37.180 --> 00:04:37.620
Mm-hmm.

115
00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:44.660
Kent Zabornak told me that we had to create all of our own signage and props for the school

116
00:04:44.660 --> 00:04:50.240
because we had to make sure, per our agreement with Birmingham High School, that none of their

117
00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:53.760
actual logos or artwork or signage was seen.

118
00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:54.960
So there you go.

119
00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:55.980
We made it all.

120
00:04:56.180 --> 00:04:57.260
Everything hanging on the wall.

121
00:04:57.400 --> 00:04:57.700
Everything.

122
00:04:58.380 --> 00:04:58.820
Wowzers.

123
00:04:58.940 --> 00:04:59.620
That's a lot.

124
00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:02.460
Listen, Kent told me that as I was watching the episode.

125
00:05:02.580 --> 00:05:04.080
I was like, that's a lot of signs.

126
00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:04.740
Yeah.

127
00:05:05.060 --> 00:05:05.560
Check it out.

128
00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:08.000
Our art department was very busy this episode.

129
00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:08.700
They were.

130
00:05:09.220 --> 00:05:11.160
I'm moving us into fast fact number two.

131
00:05:11.420 --> 00:05:12.500
It's called golfing.

132
00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:13.340
Wait, wait.

133
00:05:13.460 --> 00:05:15.120
I sense a location breakdown.

134
00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:16.680
You are correct, Angela.

135
00:05:16.900 --> 00:05:19.860
And it's because we got a fan question from Sophia D.

136
00:05:20.240 --> 00:05:23.260
Where did you film the scenes at the golf course?

137
00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:25.520
Because I'll have you notice, I looked.

138
00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:28.940
We never see a sign for where our guys are supposed to be.

139
00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:29.700
Mm-mm.

140
00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:35.000
I Googled, there is a country club of Scranton that offers golf as well as a few other golf

141
00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:36.400
courses near the Scranton area.

142
00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:42.420
I don't know which course this is supposed to be, but we filmed at Vista Valencia Golf

143
00:05:42.420 --> 00:05:43.960
Course in Santa Clarita.

144
00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:44.860
Mm-hmm.

145
00:05:44.860 --> 00:05:47.120
It's a 27-hole facility.

146
00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:53.140
It has an 18-hole par 61 course and a 9-hole par 3 course.

147
00:05:53.480 --> 00:05:55.180
Now, here's what I found very interesting.

148
00:05:55.380 --> 00:05:56.500
Maybe only to me.

149
00:05:56.760 --> 00:05:57.700
Let's hear it.

150
00:05:57.860 --> 00:06:02.780
The prices to play depend on what day you're playing and also what time you arrive.

151
00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:07.020
It's least expensive to go during the week in the afternoon.

152
00:06:07.020 --> 00:06:12.000
If you come first thing in the morning, it's going to cost you $24.50 to walk the course

153
00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:13.860
or $36.50 to ride it.

154
00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:19.440
If you come at 3 o'clock, it's only $13 to walk it and $23.50 to ride it.

155
00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:22.600
But why is it more expensive to ride it?

156
00:06:22.680 --> 00:06:24.140
Is it because it comes with the cart?

157
00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:25.620
I couldn't find that information.

158
00:06:25.820 --> 00:06:30.720
It seems like you'd float faster if you're riding it than if you're walking it.

159
00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:31.740
Guess what, everybody?

160
00:06:31.900 --> 00:06:33.160
I don't know a lot about golfing.

161
00:06:34.340 --> 00:06:36.880
This is why I'm quiet because I'm like, I don't know.

162
00:06:37.180 --> 00:06:38.780
But here's the big kicker.

163
00:06:38.900 --> 00:06:41.380
And this is why I think you and I need to go to this golf course.

164
00:06:41.620 --> 00:06:41.900
Okay.

165
00:06:42.240 --> 00:06:44.300
They have something called foot golf.

166
00:06:44.600 --> 00:06:45.460
Foot golf?

167
00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:47.060
I'd never heard of it.

168
00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:48.240
It's a real thing.

169
00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:51.040
It's a combination of soccer and golf.

170
00:06:51.320 --> 00:06:52.280
And hacky sack.

171
00:06:52.600 --> 00:06:54.860
I think you could hacky and sack it in there.

172
00:06:55.240 --> 00:06:59.260
There's basically a special golf course, but the holes are really big

173
00:06:59.260 --> 00:07:02.180
and you kick the ball down the course into the hole.

174
00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:02.920
Okay.

175
00:07:03.160 --> 00:07:03.880
Foot golf.

176
00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:06.760
Maybe we could frolf and then foot golf.

177
00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:12.020
I would foot golf if there was like a pony keg set up on like the eighth hole.

178
00:07:12.180 --> 00:07:16.080
So like you kick your ball, then you have a beer, then you kick your ball.

179
00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:17.420
What's a pony keg?

180
00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:18.680
A pony keg, isn't that?

181
00:07:18.760 --> 00:07:19.980
Don't y'all have pony kegs?

182
00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:20.900
It's like a party keg.

183
00:07:21.020 --> 00:07:22.520
It's like a mini keg of beer.

184
00:07:22.660 --> 00:07:23.380
A pony keg?

185
00:07:23.480 --> 00:07:23.700
Anyone?

186
00:07:24.320 --> 00:07:24.760
Sam?

187
00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:25.480
Cassie?

188
00:07:25.600 --> 00:07:26.120
Pony keg?

189
00:07:26.180 --> 00:07:26.720
Ever heard of it?

190
00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:29.440
A pony keg is a mini keg?

191
00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:30.080
Yeah.

192
00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:31.220
It's like a baby keg.

193
00:07:31.280 --> 00:07:31.780
No, you're right.

194
00:07:31.780 --> 00:07:33.260
Pony keg is a quarter keg.

195
00:07:33.280 --> 00:07:33.540
Yeah.

196
00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:34.420
Thank you.

197
00:07:35.040 --> 00:07:36.580
What's a half keg called?

198
00:07:38.650 --> 00:07:39.230
Silence.

199
00:07:43.360 --> 00:07:44.940
I don't find any cool names.

200
00:07:45.340 --> 00:07:46.920
Oh, so you can get up.

201
00:07:47.240 --> 00:07:48.120
Here are your choices.

202
00:07:48.360 --> 00:07:50.140
Pony keg, half keg, keg.

203
00:07:52.580 --> 00:07:56.820
I feel like they sell more pony kegs just because the name is cute, but I don't know.

204
00:07:56.820 --> 00:08:00.500
And you can carry them if you're on the petite side, like myself.

205
00:08:01.180 --> 00:08:02.860
Oh, we're learning so much today.

206
00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:03.680
So much.

207
00:08:04.200 --> 00:08:05.520
Fast fact number three.

208
00:08:05.860 --> 00:08:10.800
Angela, you were very, very, very pregnant in this episode.

209
00:08:11.140 --> 00:08:12.680
Yeah, I was.

210
00:08:13.040 --> 00:08:19.420
When you were filming your scenes with Dwight in the office, Lee Eisenberg had the flu.

211
00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:20.560
He was not there that day.

212
00:08:20.740 --> 00:08:22.600
Only Gene Stepnitsky was on the set.

213
00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:27.560
When they got into the editing bay to edit the episode, Lee Eisenberg was there and he

214
00:08:27.560 --> 00:08:31.680
said, you guys, why don't we have any wider shots of these scenes?

215
00:08:31.940 --> 00:08:38.480
And Dave Rogers and Gene had to remind him because Angela's belly was very hard to hide.

216
00:08:38.480 --> 00:08:44.640
So all of these, all of these shots are like Angela from like the shoulders up.

217
00:08:44.760 --> 00:08:47.700
But here is what else I found in my Googling, Angela.

218
00:08:48.060 --> 00:08:48.620
What?

219
00:08:49.100 --> 00:08:53.040
By the time this episode aired, you had given birth.

220
00:08:53.540 --> 00:08:54.420
I know.

221
00:08:54.820 --> 00:08:58.420
You gave birth five days before this episode aired.

222
00:08:58.760 --> 00:08:59.700
That is true.

223
00:09:00.040 --> 00:09:02.400
Well, lady, I have a really fun story from this episode.

224
00:09:02.400 --> 00:09:05.520
And it's something that involves the golf course.

225
00:09:05.860 --> 00:09:10.180
I had no scenes at the golf course, but I went to visit the fellas.

226
00:09:10.460 --> 00:09:15.240
I was doing a whole series at this time on NBC.com called Adventures with Angela.

227
00:09:15.860 --> 00:09:19.760
And Creed and Ed had written a song for my baby.

228
00:09:20.360 --> 00:09:23.540
I mean, with the banjo, the guitar, the whole thing.

229
00:09:23.760 --> 00:09:27.540
So I went to the golf course on Monday on their lunch.

230
00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:31.480
And we sat out in this beautiful green, like grassy area.

231
00:09:32.040 --> 00:09:33.540
And they sang to me.

232
00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:38.080
And not only that, I couldn't remember how we got there.

233
00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:41.380
I was like, I don't remember driving to this place or where it was.

234
00:09:41.520 --> 00:09:44.740
And you know, when you're a passenger, how you don't really pay attention as much.

235
00:09:45.160 --> 00:09:45.340
Yeah.

236
00:09:46.120 --> 00:09:50.660
So I found this email that I had written to John Krasinski, where I said,

237
00:09:50.900 --> 00:09:52.700
Hey, John, I'll see you Monday.

238
00:09:52.940 --> 00:09:53.580
I can't wait.

239
00:09:53.800 --> 00:09:55.900
Creed is picking me up in a sports car.

240
00:09:56.080 --> 00:09:56.960
Should I be scared?

241
00:09:56.960 --> 00:09:58.760
And we're going to come and have lunch.

242
00:09:58.880 --> 00:10:02.180
And he and Ed are going to sing a song for my little baby.

243
00:10:03.060 --> 00:10:06.120
Oh, so you wrote in Creed's sports car?

244
00:10:06.380 --> 00:10:09.520
I wrote in Creed's little two-seater sports car.

245
00:10:09.860 --> 00:10:11.820
And they sang this song to me.

246
00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:13.560
And it was on NBC.com.

247
00:10:13.660 --> 00:10:14.880
And Jenna, they gave me a copy.

248
00:10:14.940 --> 00:10:19.060
And I tore my house up looking for this this week.

249
00:10:19.160 --> 00:10:21.920
I have ransacked the whole house.

250
00:10:22.120 --> 00:10:23.860
I know I have it somewhere.

251
00:10:23.860 --> 00:10:25.900
And I really wanted to play it for you guys.

252
00:10:25.900 --> 00:10:30.260
But Joya, who worked with us over at NBC.com, is on the case.

253
00:10:30.440 --> 00:10:31.360
She's going to find it.

254
00:10:31.680 --> 00:10:35.940
And hopefully, maybe in a revisited, I'll be able to play it for you guys, because it's

255
00:10:35.940 --> 00:10:36.680
really special.

256
00:10:36.680 --> 00:10:39.020
And I'm just heartbroken that I couldn't find it.

257
00:10:39.020 --> 00:10:41.660
That is so cool, Angela.

258
00:10:41.960 --> 00:10:43.900
I remember seeing the video of that.

259
